// A UNIT FUNCTION WHOSE BLOCK BODY SIMPLY ENDS -- the form the corpus never carried.
//
// Why this fixture exists (2026-09-09). `emit_callable` printed a trailing return only for the
// entry row and for `int` functions, so a plain `-> ()` function with a block body got NONE: its
// C fell off the end of a function whose return type is `nova_unit`. A grep across
// `examples/basics/` and `novac/fixtures/` found zero carriers of the form, which is why every
// green measurement of wave M3 -- corpus C identical on 94 files, differential 35 of 35, module
// tests 26 of 26 -- was silent about it.
//
// The statements before the end are the point: without them a missing return is invisible,
// because there is nothing for it to skip.
//
// WHAT THIS FIXTURE DELIBERATELY DOES NOT CARRY, and the reason is a measurement: a BARE `return`
// is outside novac's subset -- the checker refuses it by name, `outside the subset: return must
// carry a value`. The first edition of this carrier had one, and the probe refused the whole file.
// So that form needs no emitter fix at all: the boundary is held by the checker, which is where a
// boundary belongs.
module bare_return.pos_1

fn hush(n int) -> () {
    println("quiet")
    println(n)
}

fn main() {
    hush(9)
    println("after")
}
